// The negative control for `tests/pass/a_scalar_may_leave_a_region_that_allocated.bx`. That fixture
// permits a scalar out of a region that allocated; this proves the permission did not widen into
// "anything may leave a region". A String CAN hold region storage, so the block's release would
// invalidate exactly what the caller was handed.
//
// Both fixtures exist because the suite was green — 106 of 106 — while stage-1 still refused the
// scalar and stage-0 had been fixed. Neither the differential nor the fixpoint could see it: they
// compare what the two compilers say about programs that EXIST, and no program in the corpus
// returned a scalar out of a region that allocated.
function build(text: String) -> String {
    region r {
        let mutable copy: String = "";
        copy = copy + text;
        return copy;
    }
}

print("k");
